acme_sre: Hey @redwood — we started seeing stuck requests and runaway token usage from the Node SDK. Node 18.16 + undici 5.12 + @redwood/sdk@1.2.0. Calls never resolve after ~30s, retries keep firing and we get duplicate charges.

sarah_csr: Sorry for the trouble. Can you paste a minimal repro and the request_id/x-request-id if available? Also roughly when this started?

acme_sre: Started after we upgraded from SDK 1.1.x to 1.2.0 last week. Here's a tiny repro (TS):
```ts
import { RedwoodClient } from '@redwood/sdk';
import { fetch as undiciFetch } from 'undici';

globalThis.fetch = undiciFetch;
const client = new RedwoodClient({ apiKey: process.env.RW_KEY });

const ac = new AbortController();
client.generate({ model: 'ggml-test', prompt: 'hi' }, { signal: ac.signal })
  .then(r => console.log('ok', r))
  .catch(err => console.error('err', err));

setTimeout(() => ac.abort(), 5000);
```

The promise never rejects after abort, and our retries still fire. Logs:
```
[2026-03-12T14:22:08Z] request_id=abc123 attempt=1 started
[2026-03-12T14:22:38Z] attempt=1 timed out, scheduling retry in 1000ms
[2026-03-12T14:22:39Z] attempt=2 started
... repeated until billing spike
```

jake_eng: Thanks — this looks like the known issue where the SDK's retry/backoff uses setTimeout and doesn't attach the user's AbortSignal to the pending delay. If the signal is aborted while waiting for the backoff, the scheduled retry still runs. That means the original aborted request keeps being retried and you see duplicates.

oliver_support: For immediate mitigation, two options:
1) Add an idempotency header on your calls (Idempotency-Key / x-redwood-idempotency-key) so retries won't create duplicate billable actions.
2) Monkeypatch a cancelable delay and pass signals through (example below) or downgrade to @redwood/sdk@1.1.x until we push a fix.

jake_eng: Example cancelable delay:
```js
function delay(ms, signal) {
  return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
    const t = setTimeout(() => { signal?.removeEventListener('abort', onAbort); resolve(); }, ms);
    function onAbort() { clearTimeout(t); reject(new Error('aborted')); }
    signal?.addEventListener('abort', onAbort);
  });
}
// In your wrapper, ensure we call delay(backoffMs, options.signal)
```

acme_sre: Large thanks — will try idempotency header. Do you have an ETA on a proper SDK fix? We can't keep downgrading indefinitely.

jake_eng: assigning to jake_eng to triage, creating INC ticket.

deploy-bot: incident INC-5721 created by sarah_csr: https://internal.incidents/INC-5721

jake_eng: We're patching the retry logic to forward AbortSignal to delay timers and to short-circuit retries when aborted. The fix will be in @redwood/sdk@1.3.0; we'll try to get a 1.2.x patch if needed. Workarounds: pass a custom fetch that correctly honors signals (undici is fine), and add idempotency keys. I'll follow up with a changelog and a code patch.

acme_sre: Thanks! Please cc when the patch is out so we can upgrade and validate before business hours.

sarah_csr: cc'd — will ping when the release is published. :thumbsup:
